{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261113T063004Z_dev-05_flat_e51d", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The paper does not report a detection significance for the GCE, either in σ or as a test statistic, so I can't give a value. It says only that the fitted GCE flux stays nonzero in all 80 diffuse-emission models, and that this \"alone does not establish its statistical significance\". It also says that differences in Δ(−2lnL) between the non-nested diffuse models cannot be read as squared Gaussian significances. The statistics it does give are χ²/dof values for DM-spectrum fits to the GCE spectrum, for example χ²_min = 27.50 for 12 dof in the b b̄ channel. These measure goodness of fit, not a detection significance.", "found": false, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.1"}]}, "turns": 9, "seconds": 23.023, "tool_calls": 8, "tool_result_chars": 306863, "input_tokens": 20, "output_tokens": 1123, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 69446, "cache_read_input_tokens": 921901, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-13T06:30:27+00:00"}
